---
components: ["FunnelBars"]
description: Funnel bars show how a count narrows across ordered stages, such as a signup or checkout flow, with the conversion rate and the drop at each step.
---

<script>
  import { Button, Stack } from "carbon-components-svelte";
  import { DeltaIndicator, FunnelBars } from "carbon-components-svelte/viz";

  const stages = [
    { id: "visit", label: "Visitors", value: 10000 },
    { id: "signup", label: "Signup", value: 6000 },
    { id: "activate", label: "Activated", value: 3000 },
    { id: "paid", label: "Paid", value: 900 },
  ];

  const baseline = { visit: 1, signup: 0.55, activate: 0.52, paid: 0.33 };

  let selectedId = "activate";
  let live = stages;

  function reshuffle() {
    let previous = 8000 + Math.round(Math.random() * 4000);
    live = stages.map((stage, i) => {
      if (i > 0) previous = Math.round(previous * (0.3 + Math.random() * 0.5));
      return { ...stage, value: previous };
    });
  }
</script>

`FunnelBars` is part of the data visualization subpackage. Import it from `carbon-components-svelte/viz` and load `carbon-components-svelte/css/viz.css` alongside `all.css`. With a single-theme stylesheet such as `g100.css`, load the matching `viz-g100.css` instead. The subpackage is experimental: its API may change in a minor release.

Stages render as rows of a table, so labels, bars, and numbers stay aligned at any width and assistive technology reads each stage as a row.

## Basic

Pass `stages` in order and set `label` to name the funnel. Bar length is relative to the largest stage.

<FunnelBars {stages} label="Signup funnel, last 30 days" />

## Rates

Set `rate` to choose which conversion rate to show. `"overall"` is relative to the first stage and `"step"` to the previous one.

### Step

<FunnelBars {stages} label="Signup funnel" rate="step" />

### Both

<FunnelBars {stages} label="Signup funnel" rate="both" />

### None

<FunnelBars {stages} label="Signup funnel" rate="none" />

## Drop-off

### Show what each stage lost

Set `showDrop` to draw the lost portion as a hatched bar with its percentage.

<FunnelBars {stages} label="Signup funnel" rate="step" showDrop />

### Highlight the largest drop

Set `highlight` to `"largest-drop"` to flag the stage that lost the most, or to a stage `id` to flag a specific one. The flag uses an icon as well as color.

<FunnelBars {stages} label="Signup funnel" rate="step" showDrop highlight="largest-drop" />

## Shape

### Centered

Set `align` to `"center"` for the classic funnel silhouette. The bar lengths are unchanged.

<FunnelBars {stages} label="Signup funnel" align="center" showDrop />

### Square root scale

A very small last stage can vanish on a linear scale. Set `scale` to `"sqrt"` to keep it visible. Because bar lengths are then no longer proportional, a "Not to scale" note is always shown.

<FunnelBars {stages} label="Signup funnel" scale="sqrt" />

## Sizes

Set `size` to control the row height.

<Stack gap={7}>
  <FunnelBars {stages} label="Small funnel" size="sm" />
  <FunnelBars {stages} label="Medium funnel (default)" />
  <FunnelBars {stages} label="Large funnel" size="lg" />
</Stack>

## Color

### Semantic or categorical

Set `color` to a semantic name, a categorical index from 1 to 14, a viz token name, or any CSS color.

<Stack gap={7}>
  <FunnelBars {stages} label="Neutral funnel" color="neutral" />
  <FunnelBars {stages} label="Categorical funnel" color={3} />
</Stack>

### Per stage

Give a stage its own `color` to override the funnel's.

<FunnelBars
  label="Signup funnel"
  stages={[
    { id: "visit", label: "Visitors", value: 10000 },
    { id: "signup", label: "Signup", value: 6000 },
    { id: "activate", label: "Activated", value: 3000 },
    { id: "paid", label: "Paid", value: 900, color: "success" },
  ]}
/>

## Formatting

Set `format` to `Intl.NumberFormat` options or a function. Values use compact notation by default.

<FunnelBars {stages} label="Signup funnel" format={{ maximumFractionDigits: 0 }} />

## Selectable

Set `selectable` to make stages interactive and bind `selectedId`. Use the arrow keys to move between stages and Enter or Space to select one. The `select` event fires on user action only.

<FunnelBars
  {stages}
  label="Signup funnel"
  rate="step"
  selectable
  bind:selectedId
  on:select={(e) => console.log("select", e.detail.stage.id)}
/>

## Slots

Use the `label`, `value`, and `rate` slots to customize a cell. Each receives `stage`, `stats`, and `index`.

<FunnelBars {stages} label="Signup funnel" rate="step">
  <svelte:fragment slot="rate" let:stage let:stats>
    {#if stats.stepRate !== null}
      <DeltaIndicator value={stats.stepRate - baseline[stage.id]} format="percent" size="sm" label="vs target" />
    {/if}
  </svelte:fragment>
</FunnelBars>

## Live data

Reassign `stages` to update. Rows are keyed by `id`, so bars animate to their new length instead of being recreated.

<Button size="small" kind="tertiary" on:click={reshuffle}>Randomize</Button>

<FunnelBars stages={live} label="Live funnel" rate="step" showDrop highlight="largest-drop" />

## Links

Give a stage an `href` to render its label as a link.

<FunnelBars
  label="Signup funnel"
  stages={[
    { id: "visit", label: "Visitors", value: 10000, href: "#visitors" },
    { id: "signup", label: "Signup", value: 6000, href: "#signup" },
  ]}
/>

## Accessibility

The funnel is a table. The caption carries `label` and the overall conversion, each stage is a row with a row header, and the bar column is hidden from assistive technology because the value and rate columns already say what it shows. Column headers are visually hidden. Set `headerLabels` to localize them. Leave `label` empty only when nearby text already conveys the same information: the whole funnel is then hidden from assistive technology.
